  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342199",
      "title": "What is Deno?",
      "lectureOrder": 516,
      "videoOrder": 457,
      "sourceHash": "2f72a832ea1b95341e8a7b3b6b28f128066ca313e18b8164bce683c68a7a7b3b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.913,
          "en": "So, what is Deno?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.783,
          "end": 8.59,
          "en": "Deno is a JavaScript runtime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.59,
          "end": 12.82,
          "en": "based on Chrome's V8 JavaScript engine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.82,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "And if you think about that sentence,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 17.23,
          "en": "if you read it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.23,
          "end": 19.82,
          "en": "it might sound quite familiar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.82,
          "end": 23.26,
          "en": "that's the same thing Node.js is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.26,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "Node.js also is a JavaScript runtime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 30.82,
          "en": "based on Chrome's V8 JavaScript engine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.82,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "So, is Deno the same thing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 35.62,
          "en": "Well, let's see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.62,
          "end": 38.59,
          "en": "Deno, since it is that JavaScript runtime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.59,
          "end": 41.91,
          "en": "allows us to run JavaScript outside of the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 43.32,
          "en": "just like Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 46.95,
          "en": "But now there are a couple of key features in Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 49.27,
          "en": "which don't exist like that in Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.27,
          "end": 53.15,
          "en": "for example, Deno is not only a JavaScript runtime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.15,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "but actually a JavaScript and TypeScript runtime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "Now I do have a whole module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 63.38,
          "en": "where I show you that you can use TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.38,
          "end": 65.44,
          "en": "with Node.js as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.44,
          "end": 67.93,
          "en": "The key difference is that for Node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.93,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "Node itself, the Node executable is only capable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 74.4,
          "en": "of executing JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.4,
          "end": 77.06,
          "en": "TypeScript code needs to be compiled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.06,
          "end": 79.28999999999999,
          "en": "to JavaScript code first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.28999999999999,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "Deno on the other hand is also an executable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 85.45,
          "en": "which is capable of executing JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.45,
          "end": 87.16,
          "en": "but it's also capable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.16,
          "end": 89.96000000000001,
          "en": "of executing uncompiled TypeScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.96000000000001,
          "end": 94.24000000000001,
          "en": "because Deno has its own built in TypeScript compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.24000000000001,
          "end": 99.24000000000001,
          "en": "Now, in addition, Deno supports URL imports out of the box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.44,
          "end": 103.92,
          "en": "and modern JavaScript features like promises are embraced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.92,
          "end": 106.45,
          "en": "Now, I do you also have that module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.45,
          "end": 108.97999999999999,
          "en": "on modern JavaScript with Node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.97999999999999,
          "end": 111.6,
          "en": "and there you learn that you can also import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.6,
          "end": 115.55,
          "en": "in a different way than used in the majority of the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.55,
          "end": 118.25,
          "en": "and that you can use promises for example, on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.25,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "some of the built in features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 123.81,
          "en": "but unlike Node, Deno embraces this concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.81,
          "end": 126.02,
          "en": "out of the box from very start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.02,
          "end": 129.46,
          "en": "simply because it's newer than Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.46,
          "end": 132.89,
          "en": "There also is something about these URL imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.89,
          "end": 135.05,
          "en": "that differs significantly from how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.05,
          "end": 137.56,
          "en": "you manage dependencies and Node projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.56,
          "end": 139.78,
          "en": "but I will come back to that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.78,
          "end": 142.89,
          "en": "And last but not least one other key difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.89,
          "end": 145.49,
          "en": "and one other key feature of Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.49,
          "end": 148.99,
          "en": "is that it's secure by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.99,
          "end": 151.36,
          "en": "Now, if you read it like this, this sounds horrible, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.36,
          "end": 154.16,
          "en": "It sounds like Node is not secure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.16,
          "end": 156.61,
          "en": "and that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.61,
          "end": 159.27,
          "en": "I'll come back to what I mean with secure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.27,
          "end": 162.32,
          "en": "and which specific aspect this is about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.32,
          "end": 164.04,
          "en": "throughout this module, and you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.04,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "that it's not that horrible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 169.57999999999998,
          "en": "but that it still might be a nice feature to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.57999999999998,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "So let's maybe now get started with Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 175.45,
          "en": "let's write some code so that we get a feeling for it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.45,
          "end": 177.07,
          "en": "and let's then step-by-step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.07,
          "end": 180.55,
          "en": "find out what the differences are compared to Node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.55,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "how you can build apps with Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 186.663,
          "en": "and in the end, let's find out whether you should switch.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
